* Set and rarity: underlying [[Captain Needa]]; the gallery face carries the Dagobah set icon.
* [[Media:Decipher_Glossary_1998.pdf|Decipher Glossary (November 1998)]], PDF page 32, earlier documentary text matching this image.
|errata_history=The gallery face has a bronze round disc at lower right, without an E or number. Its game-text words match the November 1998 Glossary entry and the later June 2017 partial and 2018 full face. The gallery rendering differs visibly in its title, lore and text layout, frame and round mark. The June 2017 partial instead prints an <code>E</code>. Before (physical Decipher face) and after (gallery face), with later PC images: [[File:Captain-Needa-PC-gallery-2007-through-2023-comparison.png|thumb|center|300px|Physical scan and five PC image versions.]]
|notes=* The archive capture establishes availability by 16 December 2007; the first publication day is not established.<ref name="gallery">[https://web.archive.org/web/20071216200322id_/http://www.swccgpc.com/cards/dagobah/ds/captainneeda.gif PC gallery capture], 16 December 2007, 20:03:22 UTC.</ref>
* Destiny, lore, power, ability, deploy, forfeit and the pilot/warrior icons above are printed on this gallery face. Set and rarity are inherited catalogue information.
* Force-Attuned is the printed sensitivity label. Under [[Media:SWCCG_2023_AdvancedRulebook.pdf|Advanced Rulebook (2023)]], PDF page 78, it is an ability-based attribute; captain and leader are characteristics supported by the lore (pages 177–178). Landspeed 1 is the character default, not a printed number ([[Media:Decipher_Glossary_1998.pdf|Glossary (1998)]], PDF page 34; Advanced Rulebook (2023), page 77).
|rulings=* The November 1998 Glossary distinguishes choosing forfeitures for battle damage or attrition from mandatory weapon-hit forfeitures.<ref name="historical-forfeit">[[Media:Decipher_Glossary_1998.pdf|Decipher Glossary Version 2.0 (November 1998)]], PDF page 32, Captain Needa.</ref>
